  "steps": [
    "Loaded 303 patients (UCI Cleveland) and decoded the numeric codes into readable categories, checking each mapping against the original UCI file (the target turned out to be inverted).",
    "Built one scikit-learn Pipeline: scaling for numbers, one-hot encoding for categories.",
    "Tuned a Decision Tree with GridSearchCV inside each fold (nested CV) and compared it with Logistic Regression and Random Forest using 5\u00d75 repeated stratified cross-validation.",
    "Picked Logistic Regression by ROC-AUC and evaluated it once on a held-out 20% test set.",
    "Visualised the tuned tree and explained the model with permutation importance.",
    "Exported the whole pipeline to ONNX so it runs in the browser \u2014 no server needed."
  ],
  "dataset": {
    "name": "UCI Heart Disease (Cleveland)",
    "url": "https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/45/heart+disease",
    "rows": 303
  },
